WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.120
Because most of the time we would take from our garden and take it down to the . . . what we used for a well and wash it,

2
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:19.460
basket it, and then my parents would take it to the store on Saturday evening and get what was needed for the house.

3
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:30.000
As to what we didn't raise -- soap, stuff what we didn't raise -- and that was calculated to see what it would come from.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.200
Then this broker would go outside and see what you had on your wagon.

5
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.240
He would count this and put a price on it.

6
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.440
And then what you owed him, he’d subtract this from it and see where it left you.

7
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.180
So you took it to a broker?

8
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.120
Well no, no. The guy who runs the store.

9
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.780
Just the man who ran the grocery store?

10
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:50.240
Yeah.

11
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:50.860
Okay.

12
00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.160
Yeah.

13
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.120
So he was buying the produce?

14
00:00:53.120 --> 00:01:02.060
He would buy what we brought and we would buy what we needed to function from the store.

15
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.280
Like we didn't make no toothpaste.

16
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.280
You just traded goods.

17
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.080
Just trade.

18
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.580
I don't remember if any money changed hands because sometimes it would be up and down.

19
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:18.640
Sometimes if we didn't have enough to what we had already taken up, well, it just rolled over.

20
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:24.870
I don't remember at any time that there was any money changed hands that I can remember, yeah.
